Package: fcitx5-slm-ime
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, fcitx5, slm-ime-server (>= ${source:Version})
Recommends: xdg-utils
Description: Japanese input method for fcitx5 using a small language model
 Engine of fcitx5-slm-ime. It turns typed romaji into hiragana, sends the
 reading and the text before the cursor to the conversion server
 (slm-ime-server), and shows the answer bunsetsu by bunsetsu with candidates.
 .
 After the installation, restart fcitx5 and add "SLM IME" to the input methods
 with fcitx5-configtool.

Package: slm-ime-server
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, libanthy1t64 | libanthy1, slm-ime-model (>= ${source:Version})
Breaks: fcitx5-slm-ime (<< ${source:Version})
Description: Conversion server of fcitx5-slm-ime (kana to kanji on a CPU)
 HTTP server on 127.0.0.1:8190 that converts hiragana to kanji-kana text with
 a small Transformer model, using the text before the cursor as context. It
 runs on a CPU. The package contains the server, its own Java runtime, the PyTorch native libraries
 that the server loads (so that it starts without network access), and a
 systemd user service that starts it at login.
 .
 The choices of the user are kept in ~/.local/share/slm-ime/user_history.tsv.

Package: slm-ime-model
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: Trained model of fcitx5-slm-ime
 TorchScript files and the tokenizer of the conversion model of
 fcitx5-slm-ime: a character-level Transformer encoder-decoder with about 60
 million parameters, trained on pairs of a reading and kanji-kana text made by
 an LLM from the Japanese Wikipedia.
